<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chera Perumals of Makotai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 800 – <a href="/years/1124">1124</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Later Cheras</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chera Perumals of Makotai were a dynasty that ruled much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a> in south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from about 800 to the early 12th century, with their capital at Makotai, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahodayapuram">Mahodayapuram</a>, near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kodungallur">Kodungallur</a>. Their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grants, such as the Syrian Christian plates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kollam">Kollam</a>, show a kingdom of chiefdoms, temple councils and active trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>. After the dynasty ended, chiefdoms such as Venad became independent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chera-perumals-of-makotai.jpg" alt="Chera Perumals of Makotai" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sundar Lakshman · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_India_in_early_11th_century_AD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
